n  files  (the\n   \"Software\"),  to  deal in  the  Software  without restriction,  including\n   without  limitation the  rights  to use,  copy,  modify, merge,  publish,\n   distribute, sublicense, and/or sell copies of the Software, and to permit\n   persons  to whom  the Software  is  furnished to  do so,  subject to  the\n   following conditions:\n\n   The above copyright  notice and this permission notice  shall be included\n   in all copies or substantial portions of the Software.\n\n   THE  SOFTWARE  IS  PROVIDED  \"AS  IS\",  WITHOUT  WARRANTY  OF  ANY  KIND,\n   EXPRESS  OR IMPLIED,  INCLUDING  BUT  NOT LIMITED  TO  THE WARRANTIES  OF\n   MERCHANTABILITY, FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE AND NONINFRINGEMENT. IN\n   NO EVENT SHALL THE AUTHORS OR  COPYRIGHT HOLDERS BE LIABLE FOR ANY CLAIM,\n   DAMAGES OR  OTHER LIABILITY, WHETHER  IN AN  ACTION OF CONTRACT,  TORT OR\n   OTHERWISE, ARISING FROM, OUT OF OR IN CONNECTION WITH THE SOFTWARE OR THE\n   USE OR OTHER DEALINGS IN THE SOFTWARE.\n\n   SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\n\n   The port to Go (queue 202e): Copyright (c) the Arbace authors, under the same MIT license.\n*/"] [89 1 "// ---- xmlparse.c lines 3395-6837: from storeRawNames through"] [90 1 "// errorProcessor ----"] [92 1 "// doc_boolXML is C's conversion of a truth value to XML_Bool ((XML_Bool)!x)."] [100 1 "// doc_boolInt is C's conversion of a truth value (a bool or a comparison) to int."] [108 1 "// doc_realloc is the Go side of a character block's REALLOC that succeeded:"] [109 1 "// a new block of size bytes holding the old block's bytes (as many as fit)."] [118 1 "/*\nInitially tag->rawName always points into the parse buffer;\n\n\tfor those TAG instances opened while the current parse buffer was\n\tprocessed, and not yet closed, we need to store tag->rawName in a more\n\tpermanent location, since the parse buffer is about to be discarded.\n*/"] [132 3 "/* Stop if already stored.  Since m_tagStack is a stack, we can stop\n\t\t   at the first entry that has already been copied; everything\n\t\t   below it in the stack is already been accounted for in a\n\t\t   previous call to this function.\n\t\t*/"] [140 3 "/* For reuse purposes we need to ensure that the\n\t\t   size of tag->buf is a multiple of sizeof(XML_Char).\n\t\t*/"] [144 3 "/* Detect and prevent integer overflow. */"] [154 4 "/* if tag->name.str points to tag->buf.str (only when namespace\n\t\t\t   processing is off) then we have to update it\n\t\t\t*/"] [160 4 "/* if tag->name.localPart is set (when namespace processing is on)\n\t\t\t   then update it as well, since it will always point into tag->buf\n\t\t\t*/"] [206 16 "/* XmlContentTok doesn't always set the last arg */"] [216 3 "/* If we are at the end of the buffer, this would cause the next stage,\n\t\t   i.e. externalEntityInitProcessor3, to pass control directly to\n\t\t   doContent (by detecting XML_TOK_NONE) without processing any xml text\n\t\t   declaration - causing the error XML_ERROR_MISPLACED_XML_PI in doContent.\n\t\t*/"] [247 16 "/* XmlContentTok doesn't always set the last arg */"] [250 2 "/* Note: These bytes are accounted later in:\n\t   - processXmlDecl\n\t   - externalEntityContentProcessor\n\t*/"] [272 40 "// LCOV_EXCL_LINE"] [310 2 "/* save one level of indirection */"] [325 13 "/* XmlContentTok doesn't always set the last arg */"] [330 22 "/* i.e. 0 bytes */"] [358 4 "/* We are at the end of the final buffer, should we check for\n\t\t\t   XML_SUSPENDED, XML_FINISHED?\n\t\t\t*/"] [404 6 "// &ch: a one-character block of its own."] [406 6 "/* NOTE: We are replacing 4-6 characters original input for 1 character\n\t\t\t\t\t *       so there is no amplification and hence recording without\n\t\t\t\t\t *       protection. */"] [428 5 "/* First, determine if a check for an existing declaration is needed;\n\t\t\t\t   if yes, check that the entity exists, and that it is internal,\n\t\t\t\t   otherwise call the skipped entity or default handler.\n\t\t\t\t*/"] [579 23 "/* token spans whole start tag */"] [639 7 "/* localPart and prefix may have been overwritten in\n\t\t\t\t\t\t   tag->name.str, since this points to the binding->uri\n\t\t\t\t\t\t   buffer which gets reused; so we have to add them again\n\t\t\t\t\t\t*/"] [644 7 "/* don't need to check for space - already done in storeAtts() */"] [725 6 "/* BEGIN disabled code */"] [726 6 "/* Suppose you doing a transformation on a document that involves\n\t\t\t\t\t   changing only the character data.  You set up a defaultHandler\n\t\t\t\t\t   and a characterDataHandler.  The defaultHandler simply copies\n\t\t\t\t\t   characters through.  The characterDataHandler does the\n\t\t\t\t\t   transformation and writes the characters out escaping them as\n\t\t\t\t\t   necessary.  This case will fail to work if we leave out the\n\t\t\t\t\t   following two lines (because & and < inside CDATA sections will\n\t\t\t\t\t   be incorrectly escaped).\n\n\t\t\t\t\t   However, now we have a start/endCdataSectionHandler, so it seems\n\t\t\t\t\t   easier to let the user deal with this.\n\t\t\t\t\t*/"] [743 6 "/* END disabled code */"] [779 4 "/* We are at the end of the final buffer, should we check for\n\t\t\t   XML_SUSPENDED, XML_FINISHED?\n\t\t\t*/"] [830 4 "/* All of the tokens produced by XmlContentTok() have their own\n\t\t\t * explicit cases, so this default is not strictly necessary.\n\t\t\t * However it is a useful safety net, so we retain the code and\n\t\t\t * simply exclude it from the coverage tests.\n\t\t\t *\n\t\t\t * LCOV_EXCL_START\n\t\t\t */"] [840 4 "/* LCOV_EXCL_STOP */"] [861 2 "/* not reached */"] [864 1 "/* This function does not call free() on the allocated memory, merely\n * moving it to the parser's m_freeBindingList where it can be freed or\n * reused as appropriate.\n */"] [872 3 "/* m_startNamespaceDeclHandler will have been called for this\n\t\t * binding in addBindings(), so call the end handler now.\n\t\t */"] [888 1 "/*\nPrecondition: all arguments must be non-NULL;\n\n\tPurpose:\n\t- normalize attributes\n\t- check attributes for well-formedness\n\t- generate namespace aware attribute names (URI, prefix)\n\t- build list of attributes for startElementHandler\n\t- default attributes\n\t- process namespace declarations (check and report them)\n\t- generate namespace aware element name (URI, prefix)\n*/"] [901 22 "/* save one level of indirection */"] [908 2 "/* lookup the element type name */"] [929 2 "/* Detect and prevent integer overflow. */"] [934 2 "/* get the attributes from the tokenizer */"] [938 2 "/* Detect and prevent integer overflow */"] [946 3 "/* Detect and prevent integer overflow */"] [953 3 "/* Detect and prevent integer overflow. */"] [968 4 "/* Detect and prevent integer overflow. */"] [976 2 "/* the attribute list for the application */"] [980 3 "/* add the name and value to the attribute list */"] [986 3 "/* Detect duplicate attributes by their QNames. This does not work when\n\t\t   namespace processing is turned on and different prefixes for the same\n\t\t   namespace are used. For this case we have a check further down.\n\t\t*/"] [1002 4 "/* figure out whether declared as other than CDATA */"] [1013 4 "/* normalize the attribute value */"] [1023 4 "/* the value did not need normalizing */"] [1032 3 "/* handle prefixed attribute names */"] [1035 5 "/* deal with namespace declarations here */"] [1043 5 "/* deal with other prefixed names later */"] [1053 2 "/* set-up for XML_GetSpecifiedAttributeCount and XML_GetIdAttributeIndex */"] [1066 2 "/* do attribute defaulting */"] [1096 2 "/* expand prefixed attribute names, check for duplicates,\n\t   and clear flags that say whether attributes were specified */"] [1100 16 "/* hash table index */"] [1103 3 "/* Detect and prevent invalid shift */"] [1104 60 "/* bits per byte */"] [1110 3 "/* size of hash table must be at least 2 * (# of prefixed attributes) */"] [1112 4 "/* hash table size must also be a power of 2 and >= 8 */"] [1124 4 "/* Detect and prevent invalid shift */"] [1125 43 "/* sizeof(nsAttsSize) * bits per byte */"] [1126 5 "/* Restore actual size of memory in m_nsAtts */"] [1133 4 "/* Detect and prevent integer overflow.\n\t\t\t * The preprocessor guard addresses the \"always false\" warning\n\t\t\t * from -Wtype-limits on platforms where\n\t\t\t * sizeof(unsigned int) < sizeof(size_t), e.g. on x86_64. */"] [1137 4 "// #if UINT_MAX >= SIZE_MAX: false on LP64, not compiled."] [1141 5 "/* Restore actual size of memory in m_nsAtts */"] [1148 16 "/* force re-initialization of m_nsAtts hash table */"] [1150 3 "/* using a version flag saves us from initializing m_nsAtts every time */"] [1151 21 "/* initialize version flags when version wraps around */"] [1161 3 "/* expand prefixed names and check for duplicates */"] [1164 23 "/* prefixed */"] [1171 18 "/* clear flag */"] [1174 6 "/* This code is walking through the appAtts array, dealing\n\t\t\t\t\t * with (in this case) a prefixed attribute name.  To be in\n\t\t\t\t\t * the array, the attribute must have already been bound, so\n\t\t\t\t\t * has to have passed through the hash table lookup once\n\t\t\t\t\t * already.  That implies that an entry for it already\n\t\t\t\t\t * exists, so the lookup above will return a pointer to\n\t\t\t\t\t * already allocated memory.  There is no opportunity for\n\t\t\t\t\t * the allocator to fail, so the condition above cannot be\n\t\t\t\t\t * fulfilled.\n\t\t\t\t\t *\n\t\t\t\t\t * Since it is difficult to be certain that the above\n\t\t\t\t\t * analysis is complete, we retain the test and merely\n\t\t\t\t\t * remove the code from coverage tests.\n\t\t\t\t\t */"] [1188 33 "/* LCOV_EXCL_LINE */"] [1212 26 "/*null terminator*/"] [1220 7 "/* Check hash table for duplicate of expanded name (uriName).\n\t\t\t\t\t   Derived from code in lookup(parser, HASH_TABLE *table, ...).\n\t\t\t\t\t*/"] [1225 33 "/* index into hash table */"] [1227 7 "/* for speed we compare stored hash values first */"] [1231 8 "/* s1 is null terminated, but not s2 */"] [1249 36 "/* append namespace separator and prefix */"] [1252 26 "/*null terminator*/"] [1258 5 "/* store expanded name in attribute list */"] [1263 5 "/* fill empty slot with new version, uriName and hash value */"] [1273 13 "/* not prefixed */"] [1274 18 "/* clear flag */"] [1278 2 "/* clear flags for the remaining attributes */"] [1290 2 "/* expand the element type name */"] [1312 45 "/*null terminator*/"] [1319 38 "/*null terminator*/"] [1321 2 "/* Detect and prevent integer overflow */"] [1328 3 "/* Detect and prevent integer overflow */"] [1347 2 "/* if m_namespaceSeparator != '\\0' then uri includes it already */"] [1349 2 "/* Detect and prevent integer overflow */"] [1354 2 "/* we always have a namespace separator between localPart and prefix */"] [1357 43 "/* replace null terminator */"] [1365 2 "// For the RFC 3986 ANBF grammar see"] [1366 2 "// https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc3986#appendix-A"] [1369 2 "// From rule \"ALPHA\" (uppercase half)"] [1373 3 "// From rule \"ALPHA\" (lowercase half)"] [1377 3 "// From rule \"DIGIT\""] [1380 3 "// From rule \"pct-encoded\""] [1383 3 "// From rule \"unreserved\""] [1386 3 "// From rule \"gen-delims\""] [1389 3 "// From rule \"sub-delims\""] [1398 1 "// addBinding's static locals."] [1400 1 "// \"http://www.w3.org/XML/1998/namespace\""] [1412 1 "// \"http://www.w3.org/2000/xmlns/\""] [1421 1 "/*\naddBinding() overwrites the value of prefix->binding without checking.\n\n\tTherefore one must keep track of the old value outside of addBinding().\n*/"] [1439 2 "/* empty URI is only valid for default namespace per XML NS 1.0 (not 1.1) */"] [1447 3 "/* Not allowed to bind xmlns */"] [1459 3 "/* Detect and prevent integer overflow */"] [1472 3 "// NOTE: While Expat does not validate namespace URIs against RFC 3986"] [1473 3 "//       today (and is not REQUIRED to do so with regard to the XML 1.0"] [1474 3 "//       namespaces specification) we have to at least make sure, that"] [1475 3 "//       the application on top of Expat (that is likely splitting expanded"] [1476 3 "//       element names (\"qualified names\") of form"] [1477 3 "//       \"[uri sep] local [sep prefix] '\\0'\" back into 1, 2 or 3 pieces"] [1478 3 "//       in its element handler code) cannot be confused by an attacker"] [1479 3 "//       putting additional namespace separator characters into namespace"] [1480 3 "//       declarations.  That would be ambiguous and not to be expected."] [1481 3 "//"] [1482 3 "//       While the HTML API docs of function XML_ParserCreateNS have been"] [1483 3 "//       advising against use of a namespace separator character that can"] [1484 3 "//       appear in a URI for >20 years now, some widespread applications"] [1485 3 "//       are using URI characters (':' (colon) in particular) for a"] [1486 3 "//       namespace separator, in practice.  To keep these applications"] [1487 3 "//       functional, we only reject namespaces URIs containing the"] [1488 3 "//       application-chosen namespace separator if the chosen separator"] [1489 3 "//       is a non-URI character with regard to RFC 3986."] [1510 3 "/* Detect and prevent integer overflow */"] [1519 4 "/* Detect and prevent integer overflow */"] [1538 3 "/* Detect and prevent integer overflow */"] [1559 2 "/* NULL binding when default namespace undeclared */"] [1567 2 "/* if attId == NULL then we are not starting a namespace scope */"] [1581 1 "/*\nThe idea here is to avoid using stack for each CDATA section when\n\n\tthe whole file is parsed with one call.\n*/"] [1594 37 "/* we are parsing an external entity */"] [1605 1 "/*\nstartPtr gets set to non-null if the section is closed, and to null if\n\n\tthe section is not yet closed.\n*/"] [1626 13 "/* in case of XML_TOK_NONE or XML_TOK_PARTIAL */"] [1640 5 "/* BEGIN disabled code */"] [1641 5 "/* see comment under XML_TOK_CDATA_SECT_OPEN */"] [1646 5 "/* END disabled code */"] [1711 4 "/* Every token returned by XmlCdataSectionTok() has its own\n\t\t\t * explicit case, so this defau